During hibernation, create_image() freezes all devices, takes a memory
snapshot, then thaws them so swsusp_write() can write the image to disk.

The dw_mci_rockchip_dev_pm_ops uses SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS which maps
.freeze = pm_runtime_force_suspend and .thaw = pm_runtime_force_resume.
This powers off the MicroSD controller during the freeze phase, and the
thaw fails to re-tune the SDR104 clock phase and reinitialize the IDMAC.

When swsusp_write() then starts block I/O writes to the MicroSD card,
the controller is in a desynced state and the DMA completion interrupt
never works, deadlocking the kernel.

Fix by setting .freeze = NULL and .thaw = NULL so the controller stays
powered on and ready during snapshot creation. The controller is idle at
this point (all processes and kernel threads are frozen), so keeping it
active is safe. The .poweroff callback still powers it down before the
system powers off, and .restore brings it back after resume.

This is a recognised pattern in the Linux kernel for storage controllers
that cannot truly get by a freeze/thaw cycle.

---
 drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc-rockchip.c
@@ -631,9 +631,19 @@ static void dw_mci_rockchip_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops dw_mci_rockchip_dev_pm_ops = {
-	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend,
-				pm_runtime_force_resume)
+	.suspend = pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+	.resume = pm_runtime_force_resume,
+	/* Bypass freeze/thaw so the controller stays ready for swsusp_write.
+	 * During hibernation snapshot create_image() freezes then thaws all
+	 * devices. The thaw fails to re-tune SDR104 phase, causing the
+	 * controller to deadlock when swsusp_write() hits block I/O.
+	 * .poweroff powers down before system shutdown; .restore gets it
+	 * back on resume from hibernation. */
+	.freeze = NULL,
+	.thaw = NULL,
+	.poweroff = pm_runtime_force_suspend,
+	.restore = pm_runtime_force_resume,
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(dw_mci_runtime_suspend,
 			   dw_mci_runtime_resume,
 			   NULL)
 };
